  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\frac{x}{2})$, the $y$-axis, and lines  $y=1$ and $y=3.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\frac{x}{2}) \\\\ {e}^{y} & =\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ x & =2{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{e}^{y}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =2({e}^{3}-{e}^{1}) \\\\  & =2({e}^{3}-e)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
